## basically zip takes multiple iterables like list and tuples and pair their elements together

list1=["a","b","c"]
list2=(1,2,3)

#to prove it can work with both tuples and list

paired = list(zip(list1,list2))

#so paired will be [("a",1),("b",2),("c",3)]

